{
  "answer": "You can declare and validate query parameters in FastAPI by declaring them in a Pydantic model and using the `Query` annotation. For example:\n\n```Python\nfrom fastapi import Query\n\nq: str | None = Query(None, alias=\"q\")\n```\n\nThis will declare a query parameter named \"q\" with a default value of `None`. You can also add additional validation and metadata to the parameter using the `alias` and `description` parameters.\n\nAs shown in [tutorial/query-param-models-1], you can create a Pydantic model to declare related query parameters and reuse it in multiple places.\n\nAdditionally, you can declare multiple path and query parameters at the same time, and they will be detected by name, as shown in [tutorial/query-params-4].",
